cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you reference or rely upon this research record or its original analyses in scholarly work, please cite this repository and the relevant original data sources where applicable"

title: "PfMSP3.1 SPAM Structural Characterisation"

type: software

authors:
  - family-names: "Alhabad"
    given-names: "Dalal"

repository-code: "https://github.com/dalalalhabad/PfMSP3.1-SPAM-Structural-Characterisation"

url: "https://github.com/dalalalhabad/PfMSP3.1-SPAM-Structural-Characterisation"

abstract: >-
  Computational research repository preserving and documenting structural
  characterisation of the SPAM domain of Plasmodium falciparum merozoite
  surface protein 3.1 (PfMSP3.1). The repository contains computational work
  originating from a 2020 Master's research project together with further
  structural investigations undertaken in 2026, including sequence analysis,
  structural modelling, molecular-dynamics analysis, protein-protein docking,
  sequence-provenance assessment, and comparison of sequence-matched
  structure predictions with experimental NMR restraints.

keywords:
  - Plasmodium falciparum
  - PfMSP3.1
  - SPAM domain
  - structural bioinformatics
  - molecular dynamics
  - protein modelling
  - protein-protein docking
  - AlphaFold
  - NMR restraints
  - malaria
